questions.question:
fetchWithRetry(api, { delayMs: 1000 }) calls api(); on failure it waits with setTimeout(delayMs) and calls api() again. This Vitest test times out after 5 seconds:

test('retries once after 1s', async () => {
  vi.useFakeTimers();
  const api = vi.fn()
    .mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error('503'))
    .mockResolvedValueOnce('ok');

  const result = await fetchWithRetry(api, { delayMs: 1000 });
  vi.advanceTimersByTime(1000);

  expect(result).toBe('ok');
});

What is the cause?

pollJob(getStatus) calls the async function getStatus(); when it resolves with 'pending', it schedules the next poll with setTimeout(poll, 1000). The test:

vi.useFakeTimers();
const getStatus = vi.fn().mockResolvedValue('pending');
pollJob(getStatus);            // first call happens immediately
vi.advanceTimersByTime(3000);
expect(getStatus).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(4);

The assertion fails: getStatus was called once. Why?
